==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|expediens}} (stem ''expedient-),'' present participle of {{term|expedire||to bring forward, to dispatch, to [[expedite]]; impers. to be profitable, serviceable, advantageous, expedient}} < {{term|ex||out}} + {{term|pes}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-expedient.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[simple|Simple]], [[easy]], or [[quick]]; [[convenient]].
#: ''Most people, faced with a decision, will choose the most '''expedient''' option.''

====Related terms====
* [[expede]]
* [[expedience]]
* [[expediency]]
* [[expedite]]
* [[expedition]]

